ice.txt containing exactly the two bytes `42` with NO trailing newline (use e.g. `printf '42' > src/price.txt`). Change nothing else.\n\nAcceptance check from the plan: \"src/price.txt exists and contains exactly 42 (proof: command, `cat src/price.txt`)\".\n\nCheck it yourself with `cat src/price.txt` and `od -c src/price.txt` (should show exactly `4 2`). Then commit the file on your worktree branch with message \"Stage 1: price\" ending with the line:\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nDon't read beyond what you need. Report in at most 10 lines: the branch name, the commit hash, what changed, and the output of the checks.","agentId":"a26ad5bbfc88fed4d","agentType":"general-purpose","toolsUsed":["Bash"],"harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"b845167afc9155fc","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage 1 (Price) is built and committed, and both checks pass.\n\n- **Branch:** `worktree-agent-a26ad5bbfc88fed4d`\n- **Commit:** `28ea058`, \"Stage 1: price\", ending with the `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` line.\n- **What changed:** I created `src/price.txt` with `printf '42'`, so it has no trailing newline. Nothing else changed, and the worktree is clean after the commit.\n- **`cat src/price.txt`:** `42`\n- **`od -c src/price.txt`:** `0000000   4   2` / `0000002`, which is exactly the two bytes `4 2`.\n\nFile: <scratchpad>/evelo-replay-2/work/.claude/worktrees/agent-a26ad5bbfc88fed4d/src/price.txt"}],"resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","totalDurationMs":6298,"totalTokens":22589,"totalToolUseCount":1,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":31},"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2033,"cache_read_input_tokens":20167,"output_tokens":387,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2033},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":38